{"step_index":1869,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T02:22:11Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-11-16T02:22:08Z sender=dfaefe40-f699-4276-8717-cb4f8030016c/task-1866 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=Task id \"dfaefe40-f699-4276-8717-cb4f8030016c/task-1866\" finished with result:\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\nTotal chapters extracted: 60\n  9781101658055_nav.xhtml 4471 Dune - Contents\n  About_the_Author.xhtml 1017 About the Author, Dune - ABOUT THE AUTHOR\n  afterword.xhtml 24804 Afterword by Brian Herbert, Dune - AFTERWORD\n  alsobyauthor.xhtml 1271 Continued, Dune - The Dune Chronicles\n  appendixI.xhtml 18091 Appendix I: The Ecology of Dune, Dune - APPENDIX I:\n  appendixII.xhtml 18063 Appendix II: The Religion of Dune, Dune - APPENDIX II:\n  appendixIII.xhtml 5865 Appendix III: Report on Bene Gesserit Motives and Purposes, Dune - APPENDIX III:\n  appendixIV.xhtml 3720 Appendix IV: The Almanak en-Ashraf (Selected Excerpts of the Noble Houses), Dune - APPENDIX IV:\n  chapter001.xhtml 23590 Chapter 01, Dune - A beginning is the time for taking the most delicate care that the balances are correct. This every sister of the Bene Gesserit knows. To begin your study of the life of Muad’Dib, then, take care that you first place him in his time: born in the 57th year of the Padishah Emperor, Shaddam IV. And take the most special care that you locate Muad’Dib in his place: the planet Arrakis. Do not be deceived by the fact that he was born on Caladan and lived his first fifteen years there. Arrakis, the planet known as Dune, is forever his place.\n  chapter002.xhtml 18514 Chapter 02, Dune - To attempt an understanding of Muad’Dib without understanding his mortal enemies, the Harkonnens, is to attempt seeing Truth without knowing Falsehood. It is the attempt to see the Light without knowing Darkness. It cannot be.\n  chapter003.xhtml 12630 Chapter 03, Dune - Thus spoke St. Alia-of-the-Knife: “The Reverend Mother must \n<truncated 1666 bytes>\nlonely figure with his light dimmed behind the glory of his son. Still, one must ask: What is the son but an extension of the father?\n  chapter007.xhtml 23185 Chapter 07, Dune - With the Lady Jessica and Arrakis, the Bene Gesserit system of sowing implant-legends through the Missionaria Protectiva came to its full fruition. The wisdom of seeding the known universe with a prophecy pattern for the protection of B.G. personnel has long been appreciated, but never have we seen a condition-ut-extremis with more ideal mating of person and preparation. The prophetic legends had taken on Arrakis even to the extent of adopted labels (including Reverend Mother, canto and respondu, and most of the Shari-a panoplia propheticus). And it is generally accepted now that the Lady Jessica’s latent abilities were grossly underestimated.\n ... and 45 more\n  chapter048.xhtml 53990 Chapter 48, Dune - He was warrior and mystic, ogre and saint, the fox and the innocent, chivalrous, ruthless, less than a god, more than a man. There is no measuring Muad’Dib’s motives by ordinary standards. In the moment of his triumph, he saw the death prepared for him, yet he accepted the treachery. Can you say he did this out of a sense of justice? Whose justice, then? Remember, we speak now of the Muad’Dib who ordered battle drums made from his enemies’ skins, the Muad’Dib who denied the conventions of his ducal past with a wave of the hand, saying merely: “I am the Kwisatz Haderach. That is reason enough.”\n  frontmatter001.xhtml 2121 Continued, Dune - PRAISE FOR THE DUNE CHRONICLES\n  next-reads.xhtml 1304 Discover your next great read! - @font-face {font-family: 'Shift Light'; font-style: normal; font-weight: bold; src: url('../fonts/Shift-Bold.otf');}\n  notes.xhtml 1335 Cartographic Notes, Dune - CARTOGRAPHIC NOTES\n  terminology.xhtml 41310 Terminology of the Imperium, Dune - TERMINOLOGY OF\n\nLog: file:///C:/Users/Eevyx/.gemini/antigravity/brain/dfaefe40-f699-4276-8717-cb4f8030016c/.system_generated/tasks/task-1866.log\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
